# Session abort — operator authorization (BINDING)

**Operator bind (2026-07-29):** arc 6328 — IDE lead wrongly aborted an in-flight
`project_ask` while CDP Opus had already commissioned cursor-auto on the bus.
Abort only killed IDE↔Cowork polling; operator-proxy work on the private request
lane continued — architecture limited damage; seat discipline did not.

## Invariant (one line)

`¬abort(session) ∧ ¬cancel(dispatch) ∧ ¬kill(execution)` from IDE/cursor lead
unless the operator **explicitly authorizes** that specific session or dispatch
in chat.

## Transport vs bus lane (BINDING — arc 6328)

Operator-proxy episodes use **two planes**; abort scope differs:

| Plane | Mechanism | What dies on `project_ask(op="abort")` |
|---|---|---|
| **Transport** | IDE `project_ask` / Jupiter converse (`execution_id`) | **Only** that polling handle + attached harvest lane for that id |
| **Bus** | CDP `agent_bus.request` on **private request thread** (`6329`-class) | **Nothing** — DIRECTIVEs, cursor-auto admits, nested cursor-sdk runs continue |

```
abort(project_ask) ≢ abort(operator-proxy arc)
commission(arc) lives on private request lane; project_ask is bootstrap + converse only
```

**IDE seat:** after mission `submit`, poll **6329-class lane** (`agent_bus` fetch/wait),
not “is `project_ask` still running?” — `active_work` empty does **not** mean operator
work stopped.

**Reconnect:** dead `execution_id` is not reopenable; warm `project_ask` submit with
same `holder` + `converse=true` may reattach Cowork CSE if lane registry still holds it;
**authoritative continuity** is always the private request thread + `mark_read` before
next `request`.

## Scope

| Session class | Examples | Forbidden without operator auth |
|---|---|---|
| **CDP / Cowork** | `project_ask(op="abort")`, converse lane teardown | **Yes** |
| **cursor-sdk** | cancel queued/running dispatch, bridge abort | **Yes** |
| **cursor-auto** | killing in-flight nested work from the wrong seat | **Yes** |
| **Agent-bus threads** | `update-thread --status closed` | **No** — closing a thread ≠ aborting in-flight substrate work |

## When blocked, uncertain, or scope changed

1. **Poll / read** — `project_ask(op="poll")`, `agent_bus` fetch/wait, dispatch thread closeout
2. **Report** — paste status into the live CDP converse session or bus; operator DISPOSITIONs or supersedes
3. **Never infer** "superseded scope", "rogue dispatch", or "wrong path" as license to abort

## Operator-owned interrupt paths (not IDE abort)

These are **operator-seat** moves — IDE does not substitute judgment:

- **Supersede** on a private `request` thread — re-`agent_bus.request` on the same thread (cdp-operator-proxy § Interrupt / supersede)
- Operator explicitly says **abort** / **cancel** / **kill** naming the execution id, dispatch id, or thread

## Anti-patterns

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| IDE aborts `project_ask` because CHECKPOINT next-step changed | Poll **bus lane**; paste advisory into live converse |
| IDE infers "no active CDP" from `active_work` empty while 6329 runs | Read private request thread — transport idle ≠ bus idle |
| IDE cancels queued cursor-sdk as "cleanup" | Report status; wait for operator authorization |
| "Session looked stale" → abort | Read terminal closeout / poll first |
| Fire duplicate dispatch then abort the first | Read WIP pointers; one commission path |
| Treat `abort(project_ask)` as undoing operator commission | Bus lane persists; supersede only on operator private thread |

